From 5ce4db753fc3bac02cc9d00e7918b2d062576415 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:32:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Renderer port 2: the frame allocator's table copies (its
 memcpy at +0x4d9f386/+0x4d9f54c, the 128-byte copy at +0x4d9f26e) mark their
 slots (VICTORY_PORT_COPIES=0: not); the fallback looks at every written page
 at every sync unless VICTORY_PORT_DESCRIPTORS_CHECK/EVERY say otherwise

Records those copies wrote were found by the fallback only, 16 pages a frame of ~290:
150-300 view records a frame on those 16 pages showed the slot's older view, so
trees, palms, signs and distant buildings came and went from frame to frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4da7c0be4aa62aeb94d54c34d07fdbe2d879dcb6)
